Overlay patch 0015 (rev2): iOS menu scale via SoH's OWN ScaleImGui.
Root cause of "menu scale does nothing" (device feedback 2026-07-12): SoH
has its own live scale system — OTRGlobals::ScaleImGui(), driven by
gSettings.ImGuiScale (preset index), ratio-tracked so changes apply LIVE —
and it overwrote the old LUS-side 0015's FontGlobalScale on boot. Fix:
multiply gSohIos.MenuScale (default 0.85) INTO ScaleImGui's target on iOS
and compare the combined float, so both the preset combobox and the iOS
slider apply immediately, no restart. Also fatter slider grabs on iOS
(fingers). Replaces the deleted LUS Gui.cpp patch.
rev3 (VR R1, VR-spec D8 / VR-DONOR-MAP §7b): the VR sim-rate override lands
HERE rather than in the VR patch series, because it must run at the very top of
GetInterpolationFPS -- ahead of this patch's own MatchRefreshRate cap -- and
this patch already owns that function's text. A separate patch inserting there
would break rev2's reverse probe in apply-overlay.sh, which is exactly the
"regenerate, do not stack, inside patch-inserted regions" rule.
Why it matters: the interpolation system divides this rate by OoT's native
20 fps to decide how many sub-frames per game tick, so in VR a mismatch makes
the fixed-timestep logic advance at the wrong wall-clock speed -- Link in fast
or slow motion. The donor flags it as "a correctness bug in waiting if missed".
The shell publishes the MEASURED headset cadence (SohImmersive.m); we never
assume 90, and an out-of-range value falls through to the normal path.

--- a/soh/soh/OTRGlobals.cpp
+++ b/soh/soh/OTRGlobals.cpp
@@ -980,14 +980,31 @@
 
 void OTRGlobals::ScaleImGui() {
     int32_t imGuiScaleIndex = CVarGetInteger(CVAR_SETTING("ImGuiScale"), defaultImGuiScale);
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0015): gSohIos.MenuScale multiplies the preset for
+    // fine phone-fit control. Comparing the combined float (not the index)
+    // keeps upstream's ratio mechanism and makes BOTH knobs apply live.
+    float scale = imguiScaleOptionToValue[imGuiScaleIndex] * CVarGetFloat("gSohIos.MenuScale", 0.85f);
+    if (scale == previousImGuiScale) {
+        return;
+    }
+#else
     if (imGuiScaleIndex == previousImGuiScaleIndex) {
         return;
     }
 
     float scale = imguiScaleOptionToValue[imGuiScaleIndex];
+#endif
     float newScale = scale / previousImGuiScale;
     ImGui::GetStyle().ScaleAllSizes(newScale);
     ImGui::GetIO().FontGlobalScale = scale;
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // Finger-sized slider grabs regardless of scale (sliders were hard to
+    // drag on device).
+    if (ImGui::GetStyle().GrabMinSize < 22.0f) {
+        ImGui::GetStyle().GrabMinSize = 22.0f;
+    }
+#endif
     previousImGuiScale = scale;
     previousImGuiScaleIndex = imGuiScaleIndex;
 }
@@ -1000,9 +1017,39 @@
